From: Site patches <site-patches@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] openwrt: suppress noisy wpa_supplicant mesh peer notifications

Install the OpenWrt module patch before make update. The module patch
adds a hostapd source patch that removes the logging call entirely, avoiding
formatting and log delivery for this message without changing mesh peering.

diff --git a/patches/openwrt/0099-ffgt-hostapd-omit-mesh-peer-notification.patch b/patches/openwrt/0099-ffgt-hostapd-omit-mesh-peer-notification.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/openwrt/0099-ffgt-hostapd-omit-mesh-peer-notification.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+From: Site patches <site-patches@localhost>
+Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: remove repetitive mesh peer logging
+
+Add a source patch removing only the informational peer notification.
+Applies to hostap commit 5ace39b0a4cdbe18ddbc4e18f80ee3876233c20b.
+
+diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/999-ffgt-omit-mesh-peer-notification.patch b/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/999-ffgt-omit-mesh-peer-notification.patch
+new file mode 100644
+--- /dev/null
++++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/999-ffgt-omit-mesh-peer-notification.patch
+@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
++From: Site patches <site-patches@localhost>
++Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
++Subject: [PATCH] wpa_supplicant: omit noisy mesh peer notifications
++
++Remove the informational message from wpa_mesh_notify_peer entirely.
++Repeated peer notifications otherwise incur message formatting and logging
++overhead. Keep beacon parsing, peer processing and error reporting intact.
++This also removes this informational message from control-interface monitors.
++
++diff --git a/wpa_supplicant/mesh.c b/wpa_supplicant/mesh.c
++--- a/wpa_supplicant/mesh.c
+++++ b/wpa_supplicant/mesh.c
++@@ -584,9 +584,6 @@
++ {
++ 	struct ieee802_11_elems elems;
++ 
++-	wpa_msg(wpa_s, MSG_INFO,
++-		"new peer notification for " MACSTR, MAC2STR(addr));
++-
++ 	if (ieee802_11_parse_elems(ies, ie_len, &elems, 0) == ParseFailed) {
++ 		wpa_msg(wpa_s, MSG_INFO, "Could not parse beacon from " MACSTR,
++ 			MAC2STR(addr));
